---
title: "16 · Your first endless reel (H3)"
lesson: "A reel is one screenplay for a chain of clips, each continuing the one before (Orrery Continue, or H3 Motion Context). Everything before the first SCENE (style, CAST, bindings) holds for every clip; each run writes one SCENE, and forever plays the second one again and again, rolling a new room every time. END ON: is how one clip ends and the next begins; $room[-1] is the room of the clip before. Wire the picks into Orrery Continue (the reel workflow under Templates → orrery has it all), set Generate to ×10 and watch the clip count up; Restart goes back to the first clip."
tags: [tutorial, h3, reel]
---
@h3 text 16:9
style: live-action, cinematic, one continuous unbroken ten-second shot, lantern light
context: 22
MUSIC: N/A

CAST
@KEEPER: an old lighthouse keeper, in a yellow oilskin coat and a knitted cap

SCENE the first room
$room = __tour/rooms__
SHOT 10s: push in, slow
@KEEPER walks slowly through $room, holding up a lantern, and stops in front of a closed door.
SFX: $room.sfx; slow footsteps
END ON: @KEEPER stands at a closed door, the lantern raised

SCENE the next room forever
$room = __tour/rooms__
SHOT 10s: push in, slow
@KEEPER opens the door and leaves $room[-1] behind, walks slowly through $room with the lantern raised, and stops in front of the next closed door.
SFX: $room.sfx; a door creaking open
END ON: @KEEPER stands at a closed door, the lantern raised
